      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "00ae88f6-fc7e-54d7-bda6-c2a1a9c697c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Pomeranian, Sporting Lucas Terrier, Japanese Spitz, Elkhounds\n- Places: Pomerania, Germany, Poland, Central Europe, Fennoscandia\n- Concepts: Spitz-type dogs, terrier type, dog breed standards, hunting\n\nFacts:\n- The Pomeranian, also called the Pom or Pom Pom, is a Spitz-type dog breed named after the Pomerania region in Germany and Poland in Central Europe.\n- The Sporting Lucas Terrier is a small dog breed of the terrier type.\n- The Japanese Spitz has varying ideal size standards around the world, but it is always larger than the smaller Pomeranian.\n- Elkhounds are a group of Fennoscandian dog breeds in the Spitz type that are used for hunting elk or moose and other large animals.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
